Source: flickos-software
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               python3
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: flickos-software
Architecture: all
# python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0: the window, GTK 3 so it follows the Arc theme.
# appstream: its apt hook keeps Debian's app catalog (DEP-11) and the system
# cache that gir1.2-appstream-1.0 reads when the index is built; the FlickOS
# image had no catalog without it.
# packagekit, gir1.2-packagekitglib-1.0: Debian apps are installed and
# removed through PackageKit, which asks polkit (no helper of our own).
# gir1.2-flatpak-1.0: Flathub apps, through libflatpak into the system
# installation. flatpak itself stays a Recommends of flickos-desktop: without
# it Software shows Debian's apps only.
Depends: python3,
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         appstream,
         gir1.2-appstream-1.0,
         packagekit,
         gir1.2-packagekitglib-1.0,
         gir1.2-flatpak-1.0,
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: flatpak
Description: Software: find, install and remove apps on FlickOS
 A window for apps, not packages: every desktop app in Debian's archive, in
 FlickOS's repository (with the community apps other developers publish
 there, built by FlickOS from their source and reviewed) and on Flathub,
 with its icon, description, screenshots and what it needs on disk before
 it is installed. An app that more than one offer shows once, with an apt
 source as the default and Flathub for the newer version. Apt apps are
 installed through PackageKit and ask for the password; Flathub apps go
 into the system installation. The front page's shelves, Made for FlickOS
 among them, come from a list FlickOS publishes.
 .
 A daily timer updates Flatpak apps and Flathub's catalog while the
 automatic updates are on. Nothing runs while the window is closed, and
 nothing is sent about its user.
